            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Work from gentlest upward: oil and a grey abrasive pad for light surface rust, a few hours in white vinegar for moderate rust, and electrolysis or a phosphoric acid remover for heavy pitting. Avoid coarse wire wheels, which remove sound metal and ruin socket fit and cutting edges."
          }
