            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Light surface rust is cosmetic and cleans off. Pitting is permanent and matters where precision does — a pitted socket grips less well, a pitted chisel back will not polish flat. Rust inside a ratchet mechanism is the serious case, because it causes skipping and is rarely noticed until it fails."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why do my black impact sockets rust but the chrome ones do not?",
