            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Black oxide and phosphate finishes are thin conversion coatings designed to flex with the steel under impact, not to seal it, so they offer far less corrosion protection than chrome plating. Anything black in your set needs a wipe of oil that the chrome sockets genuinely do not."
